Adaptive cadence leaves 3 on the work it would cost at 2 (`[ofxr] cadence_3x_exit`, on unless 0; balanced and rate
preferences only). User flight 2026-11-23 16:50 (Pimax 90 Hz, ATMOSX, deep pipeline): the same view read 16.5 ms of
work at 2 and 20.7 ms at 3 (busy time per frame grows at the lower rate; +1.4 to +8.4 ms over every 2 -> 3 of the
flights), so the 18.9 ms (0.85 of two periods) a return to 2 asks was never met: 95 % of the mission at 3, 28 fps,
where 2 held 45 whenever it was reached; and four of the five returns went back up within a second on the switch's
own late frames, each able to double the next stay at 3. CadenceConfig::three_exit_learned (CadenceController::
set_three_exit_learned): the work at 3, a whole window past three_settle, less the work at 2 behind the move up is
the excess (0 to 4 ms, per scene); a return to 2 asks for at most 0.85 of two periods once it is taken off (never
more than up_fraction, 0.95, in all); until measured, 0.90 of two periods. Slots missed in the first 300 ms after a
3 -> 2 send nothing to 3 and double no run. Steady, and `cadence_3x_exit=0`, keep the rule before. New tests in
latency_control_tests (cadence_3x_exit_tests): the 16:50 replay stays at 3 with the old rule and returns to 2 for
good with the new one; work that needs 3 keeps it; the unmeasured limit; misses past the settle still go to 3.

